e "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315916} {:answer/id #uuid "cc610ca7-4121-59bb-8b6e-2e667e4b319e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316276} {:answer/id #uuid "f24b10d1-1646-5236-ba37-c6e42ab5dac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316469} {:answer/id #uuid "f8779403-3b1c-590e-a881-326314ab16ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316506}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186315537} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8cf181a-e3d2-5269-b318-b692a92a9f47" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316983}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "01fa87ea-c90a-5da0-b692-1e4e4dbca851" :question/math-academy-id "q-343339" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4x$ defined on $[-1,1).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2$-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)=-2{x}^{2}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=1$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-1,1).$ \nTherefore, the $2$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-4t)\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [-2{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi t)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -2{x}^{2} & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "39822680-80da-5f81-9803-335e6ef154f4"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447646 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d5e60e-7f26-5a6e-af43-a4123987b83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447484} {:answer/id #uuid "36ace1c9-2f52-5838-8105-d6761b6f44e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447502} {:answer/id #uuid "73b3831c-2550-547a-9666-08932392aa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447537} {:answer/id #uuid "b6477d72-545a-55fc-9970-dbb46ef4dc84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2n\\pi x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447570} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3c6f01-d506-5569-bd88-65579a986ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447576} {:answer/id #uuid "fda62ace-a6e8-57a0-8947-9301332fd088" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447599}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447537} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d2f5938-a945-5655-85a1-9df429194aed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44dc124c-8bd5-5c2b-9968-0948e0b12ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447508} {:answer/id #uuid "a5a3a5a9-0a82-5630-aeb2-18f2ccb9624f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{64(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447566} {:answer/id #uuid "bf50913b-5ac2-56b3-b72d-69f38936fc45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447573} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8bfdf2-21f9-521d-9608-9f449b09f43c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447593}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447593} :answer-field/id #uuid "28452a53-092e-519f-8707-b42d65bf6fbf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f8cc8df-93da-5fc5-90b5-0a9aea8b64d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447562} {:answer/id #uuid "fedcea71-fd19-5e3b-b940-f19715b86639" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447600}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447562} :answer-field/id #uuid "7efb2097-cd14-54a1-b0fa-f72890b9e249" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447608} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01a312a5-7291-51cb-8dd7-289ffb878a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "piecewise smooth" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447479} {:answer/id #uuid "1f198c8b-d39c-5f1c-a2c3-3a8a13946bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447491} {:answer/id #uuid "86b167f0-92a0-5d4f-806f-40c507d9d0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "piecewise linear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447549}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447479} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf744a44-3007-5aee-a43d-ad3854082722" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447617} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64124e72-d81b-5c9d-8805-28e34c25a654" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447531} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b932a2-1509-5853-8fde-7217043006a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447574} {:answer/id #uuid "ddd870da-d467-558a-b3cb-54886b7718ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447585}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447531} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1109bc7-547a-500f-b40b-e4d37aec3c09" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447621}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d5d0172c-6e34-5d1d-9e31-e326cbe0c123" :question/math-academy-id "q-341195" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1$ defined on $[-2,2).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $4$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-8x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-4{x}^{2}+1∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-8x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=2$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{13}{3}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-2,2),$\n\n- continuous on $[-2,2),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-2)=F(2),$ if we extend the value at $x=2$ using the formula $F(x)=-4{x}^{2}+1.$\n\nTherefore, the $4$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4{x}^{2}+1) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{13}{3})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{64(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-32(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}) \\\\ -8x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{32(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6c9ca774-b4f6-520b-b234-3903b9ac3e3c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447647}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447647 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ee7e427-46c3-5aed-9b19-381c6b43ae67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447524} {:answer/id #uuid "84d02c9f-09db-5f84-8395-ecb31c424496" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447546} {:answer/id #uuid "d0cf8966-1bef-51d6-8f2d-fa9d3c63371e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447577} {:answer/id #uuid "d80d207a-d991-5083-a552-3b5c5c3785d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447582} :answer-field/id #uuid "831873f5-dc3b-537b-bd1b-71e87ec289b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186220905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "333c0e0a-3cd4-59b2-92d6-93fd825879e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "periodic" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447500} {:answer/id #uuid "8dfe4bcc-fec4-5ff7-a0df-23a90cd726d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "piecewise smooth" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447554} {:answer/id #uuid "91d47c98-f7da-5274-8d04-afef06f100ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "piecewise linear" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447557}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447554} :answer-field/id #uuid "b43e7061-be31-5cbe-bf03-ef1f6f83c160" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447615} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236dfc34-4dba-5219-acac-2997b2644b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447493} {:answer/id #uuid "59ad1058-0ebc-5235-bf5a-82c369a6cdde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447520}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447520} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9c3a9ee-8984-5450-8ce4-4d60f9ef3558" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447616} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043c9e6c-3a11-5aaf-8219-a664d47467a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447482} {:answer/id #uuid "4d43900b-7876-5b97-8e02-78af5f282635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447512} {:answer/id #uuid "f2b6495b-9492-557a-ad44-08522dcba0d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447595}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447595} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef7b60fb-4d25-5d6e-aabc-ba323132e09c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447625} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049f5769-5fd9-5a84-b0cd-5f4a4a5f43f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447483} {:answer/id #uuid "6552293c-ef9b-5d65-a476-a37433b05e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14(-1)^{n+1}}{n}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447532} {:answer/id #uuid "86e73d39-0624-56f2-a8d1-76729f74462b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447550} {:answer/id #uuid "99e364a6-757e-5bd5-8586-8ffbdfd41393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447561}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f55713f6-e85d-551a-86cb-466027170f89" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447626}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b5d5810a-d922-539c-8f81-743a41d8a84a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343315" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $G(x)=7x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3∼3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n7x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ),$\n\n- continuous on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-\\pi )=F(\\pi ),$ if we extend the value at $x=\\pi $ using the formula $F(x)=\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{7}{2}{x}^{2}+3) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3+\\frac{7{\\pi }^{2}}{6})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)) \\\\ 7x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{14(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot (-n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)) \\\\ 7x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-14(-1)^{n}}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ 7x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{14(-1)^{n+1}}{n}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "90354e30-ad99-522d-adc0-19a8645a92ab" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447645}}] :activity/title "Differentiating and Integrating Fourier Series" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447476}]}
